Subject: [PATCH] Preserve help action lifecycle connections when replacing its handler

Only replace triggered handlers when routing the handbook action to the
Krita manual. A blanket disconnect also removes destroyed and other
bookkeeping connections and is diagnosed by recent Qt versions.

Related upstream issue (wildcard-disconnect diagnostics and log-docker
reentrancy): https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=509947
This changes the disconnecting caller, not the upstream log-handler fix.

diff --git a/libs/ui/KisMainWindow.cpp b/libs/ui/KisMainWindow.cpp
--- a/libs/ui/KisMainWindow.cpp
+++ b/libs/ui/KisMainWindow.cpp
@@ -572,8 +572,8 @@
 
     // KDE' libs 4''s help contents action is broken outside kde, for some reason... We can handle it just as easily ourselves
     QAction *helpAction = actionCollection()->action("help_contents");
-    helpAction->disconnect();
-    connect(helpAction, SIGNAL(triggered()), this, SLOT(showManual()));
+    disconnect(helpAction, &QAction::triggered, nullptr, nullptr);
+    connect(helpAction, &QAction::triggered, this, &KisMainWindow::showManual);
 
 #if 0
     //check for colliding shortcuts
